This sample policy uses the snapshot operation to take a snapshot of an index as soon as it
contains at least one document. repository is the name of the manual snapshot repository you
registered in Amazon S3. snapshot is the name of the snapshot. For snapshot prerequisites and
steps to register a repository, see the section called “Creating index snapshots”.
{
"policy": {
"description": "Takes an index snapshot.",
"schema_version": 1,
"default_state": "empty",
"states": [{
"name": "empty",
"actions": [],
"transitions": [{
"state_name": "occupied",
"conditions": {
"min_doc_count": 1
